# OpenCode iOS port patch -- 0013
# Title: iOS line REPL turn lifecycle: fresh server connection per turn + transport retry
# Upstream: anomalyco/opencode @ e8238bae9b807b72ecfc75afd3a9fe2e6b07b944 (v2.2.5)
# Requires: patches 0001-0012 applied first.
# Files: packages/cli/src/ios-repl.ts, packages/cli/src/commands/handlers/default.ts,
#        packages/cli/src/commands/handlers/mini.ts, packages/cli/src/run/run.ts,
#        packages/cli/src/services/standalone.ts
# Why (device-reported): the patch-0012 REPL resolved its server ONCE and reused the same resolved
#      connection for every turn. After the first device turn the transport died ("Transport:
#      terminated"), later turns failed with "Transport: fetch failed" and the mock provider received
#      no further requests - the shared client/server state was poisoned. Headless `opencode run`
#      works because each process resolves and consumes a fresh connection. Fix:
#      - the REPL now takes a `resolveServer()` closure and re-resolves a fresh connection for every
#        turn (and retry). With --standalone each turn gets its own private stdio server; the
#        endpoint exposes a `close()` (ends the stdin lease and kills the owned child) so servers are
#        disposed after the turn. With the managed service it re-discovers/reconnects per turn.
#      - one automatic retry per turn on transport-class errors (transport/fetch failed/terminated/
#        socket/ECONNRESET/EPIPE/network), with a short "Retrying turn..." line; the run pipeline
#        gained an internal onError callback so the REPL can classify failures (headless reporting
#        is unchanged).
#      - the first prompt now waits for a healthy resolution (it is resolved lazily inside the turn),
#        so a not-yet-ready server cannot fail the first turn.
# Test: host mock OpenAI-compatible server (3 consecutive turns, induced abort to exercise retry);
#       device PTY test with --standalone mock provider.
# Status: iOS-only; non-iOS behavior unchanged.

